    "media:imagetext": "May\nEighteenth,\n19\n2%.\nSouth San Francisco Land \u0026 Improvement Co.,\nMerchants\nExchange Bldg.,\nSan Francisco.\nGentlemen:\nAttention: Mr. P. J. Shaw,\nGeneral Manager\nCity and County of San Francisco would like to locate on your\ndata.\nThe work will be in charge of men assigned from the United\nStates Weather Bureau and the period of observation will be from\nJuly 1, 1927, to June 30, 1928.\nIt is our desire to commence the\nconstruction of the necessary building and installation of the\nnecessary instruments immediately.\nWe would appreciate very much permission from your Company\nto locate the meteorological station on Belle Air Island, as per\nthe mao enclosed, with the privilege oi access to the same.\ncourse, it would be understood that in the event that you sold this\nd that®\nproperty before June 30, 1928, that the privilege would cease, and\nthat upon a thirty day notice\nfrom you that we would remove the\nstructure.\nWe also desire\nthe privilege of removing the structure\nand instruments at the expiration of the observation period.\nThanking you in advance for any courtesies you may extend\nto us, I am\nVery truly yours,\nRIGHT OF WAY AGENT.\nJJP: KH",
    "media:imagetext_created": 1787959475,
